l"},{"Sha":"f2858a42ba17fba1e3376440e8f3aae2aa64ca61","Login":"adamdotdevin","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Adam","AuthorEmail":"2363879\u002Badamdotdevin@users.noreply.github.com","Date":"2026-02-19T17:36:32+00:00","Message":"chore: cleanup"},{"Sha":"3c21735b35f779d69a5458b1fa5fada49fb7decb","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-02-19T17:33:56+00:00","Message":"refactor: migrate from Bun.Glob to npm glob package\n\nReplace Bun.Glob usage with a new Glob utility wrapper around the npm \u0027glob\u0027 package.\nThis moves us off Bun-specific APIs toward standard Node.js compatible solutions.\n\nChanges:\n- Add new src/util/glob.ts utility module with scan(), scanSync(), and match()\n- Default include option is \u0027file\u0027 (only returns files, not directories)\n- Add symlink option (default: false) to control symlink following\n- Migrate all 12 files using Bun.Glob to use the new Glob utility\n- Add comprehensive tests for the glob utility\n\nBreaking changes:\n- Removed support for include: \u0027dir\u0027 option (use include: \u0027all\u0027 and filter manually)\n- symlink now defaults to false (was true in most Bun.Glob usages)\n\nFiles migrated:\n- src/util/log.ts\n- src/util/filesystem.ts\n- src/tool/truncation.ts\n- src/session/instruction.ts\n- src/storage/json-migration.ts\n- src/storage/storage.ts\n- src/project/project.ts\n- src/cli/cmd/tui/context/theme.tsx\n- src/config/config.ts\n- src/tool/"},{"Sha":"56dda4c98c209a96967f045988e17486d616269f","Login":"adamdotdevin","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Adam","AuthorEmail":"2363879\u002Badamdotdevin@users.noreply.github.com","Date":"2026-02-19T17:10:47+00:00","Message":"chore: cleanup"},{"Sha":"6b8902e8b91a7561d57f80249feada949c4d0665","Login":"adamdotdevin","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Adam","AuthorEmail":"2363879\u002Badamdotdevin@users.noreply.github.com","Date":"2026-02-19T16:23:15+00:00","Message":"fix(app): navigate to last session on project nav"},{"